  • (high) Incorrect switch expression in mvx_v4l2_vidioc_dqbuf [assets/kernel/vpu/src/driver/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c:1983]
      In `mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c`, the code changes `switch (vb->type)` to `switch (vb->memory)`. However, the case labels are `V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP` (and presumably others like `V4L2_MEMORY_USERPTR`). While this change correctly aligns the switch expression with the memory type constants, it is critical to verify that `vb` (of type `struct vb2_v4l2_buffer`) actually contains a `memory` field. In standard Linux V4L2/videobuf2 headers, the buffer structure used in dqbuf typically tracks the memory type via the queue or the buffer's internal state; if `vb->memory` is not a valid member of the specific struct being used here, this will cause a compilation failure.
